# What the sdist carries, stated rather than inherited.
#
# setuptools' default sdist quietly swept `tests/test_*.py` in — but not `harness.py`,
# not `mutation_report.py`, and not `tests/adversarial/`. The result was 25 test modules
# that cannot import their own helpers: a test tree that looks shipped and cannot run is
# worse than one that is absent, because someone will try it and conclude the tool is
# broken. `ci/check-artifact-contents.py` is what caught it.
#
# So the suite is pruned. It lives in the repository, runs from there, and is not part
# of what a `pip install` is for. The artifact's own self-check is `xcheck selftest`,
# which is embedded in the package and does ship.
prune tests
prune ci
prune docs
prune skills
prune launchers
prune templates
prune .github
prune .claude-plugin
prune .codex-plugin

# The four documents an installed copy genuinely needs. Each is on the allowlist in
# `ci/check-artifact-contents.py` with the reason it is there; that file and this one
# have to agree, and the gate is what notices when they do not.
include README.md
include LICENSE
include CHANGELOG.md
include SECURITY.md
include XCHECK.md
